WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.101 line:92%
-Welcome to the show, Bowen.

00:00:01.101 --> 00:00:03.169
-Hi! Thank you for having me
-I'm so happy you're here.

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:04.104 line:92%
-I'm very happy to be here, wow.

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:06.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And this is -- this is
a workday for you.

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:08.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's a workday.
-This is the Monday pitch day.

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:10.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
And when I first met you,
when I hosted,

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
you were a writer on the show.
-Yes.

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:13.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then you became
a cast member.

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:15.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
You had auditioned before
you became a writer.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:17.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, a few times.
-And what did you --

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:19.219 line:92%
What were your audition pieces

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:21.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So I never thought it
would happen,

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:22.756 line:92%
so I just had fun with it.

00:00:22.756 --> 00:00:27.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I would do just like
really -- just silly people.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.095 line:92%
I did my soul cycle instructor

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:30.964 line:92%
I did the choking poster guy

00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:31.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:34.534
-And then they would ask you
to do impressions every time

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:35.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I had to go back in

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:37.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
a few times, and then I --
at a certain point

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:40.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just ran out of Asian
public figures.

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:41.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:44.844
-So then I really, like, scraped
the bottom of the barrel

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:47.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I did, like,
Michiko Kakutani.

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:49.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do people know who she is?
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:51.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A "New York Times"
book reviewer.

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:52.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
-Yeah.

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:54.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you, Seth.
-And was like -- I mean,

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:55.588 size:75% position:38% line:92%
ripe for the taking.

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:57.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So ripe. She --
-And I mean,

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:59.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
for years Lorne would be like,
"We don't have --"

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:00.593 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-"Where's Michiko?"

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:03.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
Who's going to use the wor
"limn" in a sketch?

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:05.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]
Um, she --

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:06.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
So the thing about
her is that she was never --

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:09.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
she's never really been
photographed, and no one knows

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:10.170 size:78% position:39% line:92%
what she sounds like.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Perfect for an impression
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:15.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But, it gave me free reign to
do whatever I wanted.

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:17.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, there you go.
-So it was great. It was fun

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:21.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One of your first character
you did on the show was,

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:23.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess, the minister of trade
yes?

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:24.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-The Trade Daddy.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Trade Daddy. Yeah. Chen Biao.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:28.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How did this -- how did thi
come to pass?

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:32.125
-This was -- this was part o
my, I think -- one of my -

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:34.527
in one of my auditions,
I did him right as the trade war

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:36.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
was starting, and I was like
"It feels topical,

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:38.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
but, like, how do you make
this funny?"

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:41.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then really the only way
to do that is

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.870
just to make him catty and mean.
-Yeah.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So that's just who he is.
-It paid off.

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:48.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
You -- you also --
this was before

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:49.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
you were a full cast member.
-Yes.

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:52.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You played Kim Jong-Un.
-Yes.

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:53.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:54.380 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-K.J.U., K.J.U.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
-K.J.U. He loves it, right
-He loves it.

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:58.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He loves it, right?
Yeah.

00:01:58.518 --> 00:01:59.552 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you -- but this is
fantastic.

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:03.223
Because again, this was before
you were a full cast member,

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:06.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
so you also had a sketch
that you'd written in the show

00:02:06.493 --> 00:02:07.193 size:75% position:38% line:92%
independent of this.

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:09.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was going through, like
a super-long dry spell.

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:11.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
When you first start out
as a writer,

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:12.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're just getting
your bearings.

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:14.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you don't really get stuff
on, and that's fine.

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:16.970
It's part of, like, the crucible
you have to walk through.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:19.172 size:88% position:44% line:92%
But then that show, I --

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:21.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
I helped write two
pretaped sketches

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:23.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was helping
on her monologue.

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:25.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was the busiest,
busiest --

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:27.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
I haven't had as busy of a wee
as that since.

00:02:27.881 --> 00:02:30.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, even as a cast member.
And we did this.

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:33.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was in my Kim Jong-Un,
and then had to run

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:35.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
under the bleachers during
dress rehearsal.

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:37.524 size:88% position:44%
So, when you're writing
a sketch, you have to go

00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:40.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
sit next to Lorne,
under the audience,

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:41.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he's watching and he's
giving you notes.

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:43.963
He's like, "Maybe we could cut
to Kenan sooner," or something

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:45.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:49.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I was still
in the full K.J.U. -- fit.

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:53.106
And then just, like, sat next to
him while he was, like,

00:02:53.106 --> 00:02:55.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
giving me feedback
and I was like, "Yeah, uh-huh.

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:57.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But that's the only way
Lorne respects you

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:59.379
is if you dress like a dictator.
-Absolutely.

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:00.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Absolutely.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's like, "You could do --
or not."

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:03.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Or not.
Just depending on -- yep.

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:05.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's up to you today."
-Exactly.

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:07.520 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:11.191
-You -- also, that was --
Sandra Oh hosting was --

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:11.724 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:13.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...just exciting
in its own right.

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:15.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
But she was a big deal for you
yeah?

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:16.095 line:92%
-She was a big deal for me

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:19.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
I remember seeing her
in "The Princess Diaries"

00:03:19.098 --> 00:03:21.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
and thinking,
"Who is that woman?"

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:23.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I stumbled on an
episode of "Arli$$"

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:25.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was like,
"Okay, this is not

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:27.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
age-appropriate for me
as a child."

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And then --

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:32.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, like, watched
"Grey's Anatomy" and thought

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:34.147 line:92%
"Oh, I'm gonna be a doctor."

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:35.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just because of Sandra Oh
playing one on TV?

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:37.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just because of --
absolutely.

00:03:37.784 --> 00:03:39.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And then, really,

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:42.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's an example of
bad representation,

00:03:42.322 --> 00:03:44.290 line:92%
because it tricks Asian people

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:47.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
into going into
the medical field.

00:03:47.427 --> 00:03:49.229 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:49.662 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:51.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
-When they should be doing
something else.

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:53.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Now I do want to point out,

00:03:53.099 --> 00:03:57.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, people you grew up aroun
had some ideas that this

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:59.505 size:75% position:38%
was going to happen.
This is really cool.

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:02.809
Your superlative was
"Most likely to be a cast member

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:04.877
on 'Saturday Night Live.'"
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:06.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's kinda crazy.
That's wild.

00:04:06.613 --> 00:04:08.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's really --
-It's weird.

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:10.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So...
-It's weird.

00:04:10.183 --> 00:04:12.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like, if I'm doing
the math right,

00:04:12.619 --> 00:04:14.554 line:92%
you had a 10-year reunion.

00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:16.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you get to go?
-I did not go,

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:19.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
because our student body
class president

00:04:19.092 --> 00:04:21.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
is nowhere to be found.
-Oh, no.

00:04:21.394 --> 00:04:22.595 line:92%
-So, I hope he's doing okay.

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:25.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
Zach Glenn,
if you're doing okay,

00:04:25.698 --> 00:04:28.301 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
please let us know?

00:04:28.301 --> 00:04:29.736 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.736 --> 00:04:30.737 line:92%
But no, it never came together

00:04:30.737 --> 00:04:34.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I would have loved to go
-Well, it's really --

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:35.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's really sweet...
-Yeah.

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:37.944
-...that they -- the fact --
like, you have to see them again

00:04:37.944 --> 00:04:41.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
collectively, because they wil
feel so right.

00:04:41.314 --> 00:04:43.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-Like, no one --

00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:44.150 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Got it.

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:45.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...no one who writes
superlative --

00:04:45.218 --> 00:04:46.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, at Donald Trump's
high school, it wasn't like,

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:48.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Most likely to be
impeached," you know?

00:04:48.855 --> 00:04:50.590 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Sure, sure, absolutely.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:52.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
They should all be
agents or something.

00:04:52.725 --> 00:04:53.626 line:92%
-They should all be agents now

00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:56.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
You -- so you were born
in Australia --

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:58.197 size:75% position:38%
grew up in Colorado,
born in Australia.

00:04:58.197 --> 00:05:00.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. And then Montreal
was in between.

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:02.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
So my dad and my mom
met in China,

00:05:02.669 --> 00:05:03.703 line:92%
then they moved to Brisbane.

00:05:03.703 --> 00:05:07.407
Was born there with my sister,
and then we moved to Montreal,

00:05:07.407 --> 00:05:08.541 line:92%
and then we moved to Denver.

00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:11.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I've lived in all these
places that used to be

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:12.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
owned by England.
-Yeah.

00:05:12.745 --> 00:05:15.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm a little Commonwealth
baby. Yeah.

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:17.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-So your parents are Chinese

00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:19.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are they -- were they excite
when they heard

00:05:19.719 --> 00:05:20.520 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
